{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A schedule holds the systems of one frame or step of a simulation. You build it by listing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the systems in a closure, and run it on a world with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which runs each system once:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 2, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 4.0, y: 70.0)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Ordering-Systems","text":"Ordering Systems","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or before one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written earlier, by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its written place:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to throw","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","text":"Running Systems at the Same Time","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two systems ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"conflict","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time. The world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order, except that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on how they happen to be written. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},{"type":"text","text":" lists those pairs, so a test can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keep a schedule free of them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L100"},"title":"Schedule","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"symbol"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Creating a Schedule","anchor":"Creating-a-Schedule","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"]},{"title":"Running Systems","anchor":"Running-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)"]},{"title":"Ordering and Conditioning Every System","anchor":"Ordering-and-Conditioning-Every-System","identifiers":